CITLY in both the per-role deny rows and the cross-tenant engine deny loop, because CapDeploy (which CI holds) is its own axis — neither CapWrite nor CapAdmin. The "scoped key planted in a foreign home org" engine assertion (a principal whose home org is org_sibling but whose grant scope still names a project in org_acme, authorized against org_sibling's resource) is independent of CapAdmin/CapWrite/CapRead — the engine refuses to consider the grant at all because the principal's OrganizationID no longer matches the grant scope's OrganizationID. Pin this on every grant-containment test so a stolen scoped key documentedly cannot be smuggled across tenants by anyone who finds it.
