st-body leak guard (anchored on caller-supplied MATRIX_KEY/matrix_value that never appear in the canonical fixture) AND a would-have-returned-data leak guard (postWriteProjectVariablesBodyLeak, anchored on the seeded post-write rows: per-row ids, keys, the non-secret value AND every recognisable fragment of the seeded secret plaintext post-write-plaintext-correcthorsebatterystaple). The allow-path Sentinel-projection assertion is the chokepoint anchor: even right after a customer submitted a secret, the post-write re-read STILL redacts via projectVariableOf -> output.Sentinel, so PUT cannot leak a secret value the customer just submitted. Forward-applicable to every future CapWrite-on-{X}-resolver matrix at any scope — keep the role / disabled / wrong-org / grant-containment skeleton + dual-direction leak guard, swap the action+resolver target+resource Kind, and ALWAYS add a secret-plaintext needle to the post-write leak guard plus a Sentinel-projection assertion on every allow-path tie-in.

