ralph/prd.json:2699:      "notes": "Implemented GET /v1/organizations/{org_id}/limits. Returns effective quota limits resolved as organization override beats plan default in one SQL statement; wire fields are resource, limit_value, enforcement_mode, source ('organization' or 'plan_default'). Resources with no policy at either scope are omitted. New store.LimitsReader composes QuotaRepository.ListEffectiveLimits through Store.Read with a pluggable PlanLookup (DefaultPlan fallback). Action limits.read authorized via organizationIDResolver against {org_id}; reader-port pattern threaded NewHandler -> newRouteTable -> handler closure. Contract tests cover success, empty list, path-org_id forwarding, 401 unauthenticated, 403 cross-tenant, 503 store outage, and nil-reader internal error. Store integration tests cover precedence resolution, empty result, tenant scoping, default vs custom PlanLookup, and nil-store rejection."
ralph/prd.json:2706:        "httptest coverage asserts GET /v1/organizations/{org_id}/limits success envelope, error envelope, request_id propagation, and OpenAPI operation registration.",
ralph/prd.json:2718:      "notes": "Contract coverage for GET /v1/organizations/{org_id}/limits."
ralph/prd.json:2722:      "title": "Add policy matrix coverage for GET /v1/organizations/{org_id}/limits",
ralph/prd.json:2737:      "notes": "Authorization coverage for GET /v1/organizations/{org_id}/limits."
ralph/prd.json:2756:      "notes": "Implemented: PATCH /v1/organizations/{org_id}/limits upserts organization-scoped quota policies. Request body: {limits:[{resource,limit_value,enforcement_mode?}, ...]} validated by httpapi (missing limit_value -> 400) and by the store layer (closed-set resource, non-negative limit, closed-set mode, no duplicates). Required action limits.write (CapAdmin, no support cross-tenant exception). Store-layer LimitsService composes a tenant existence pre-check (typed NotFound on missing org), one organization-scoped quota_policies upsert per entry, an immutable audit record (action=limits.write, metadata.updated_resources=sorted closed-set names), and an in-tx re-read of effective limits — all in one Store.Write. New QuotaRepository.UpsertOrganizationPolicy uses ON CONFLICT (organization_id, resource) WHERE scope_kind='organization' to target the partial unique index. Wired through NewHandler/newRouteTable as a new LimitsUpdater port; the route uses organizationIDResolver so cross-tenant {org_id} is a 403 before the handler runs. cmd/yalla-api builds the LimitsService at startup."
ralph/prd.json:2763:        "httptest coverage asserts PATCH /v1/organizations/{org_id}/limits success envelope, error envelope, request_id propagation, and OpenAPI operation registration.",
