diff --git a/ralph/progress.txt b/ralph/progress.txt
index a5e376391e545a1702a45f65c1f546f5671a2f2b..df0bf5c728f2717e87b7a7cc01a05c4009c5446b
--- a/ralph/progress.txt
+++ b/ralph/progress.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 ## Codebase Patterns
+- Metered overage hooks run at the usage-counter aggregation boundary, not inside quota/resource mutation code: runtime entitlement resolution carries plan/subscription metadata, `UsageCounterRepository.AggregateUsageEvents` stamps `usage_counters` with `entitlement_key`, `overage_policy_mode`, `overage_decision`, included/overage quantities, and an audit event, and `BillingExportRepository.Prepare` snapshots those fields into `billing_export_items` so provider adapters can bill/review overages without changing quota code.
 - Production operations command artifacts should follow the same static-release-gate pattern as Kubernetes/systemd artifacts: keep `deploy/operations/<command>.sh`, `deploy/operations/README.md`, `cmd/yalla-api`/`cmd/yalla-worker` entrypoint support, SECURITY.md, CI, `scripts/verify.sh`, and `internal/release/*_static_test.go` in lockstep; dry-run paths must work without production secrets and print only redacted environment names.
 - Single-node systemd operations artifacts should follow the same static-release-gate pattern as Kubernetes artifacts: keep `deploy/systemd/yalla-api.service`, `deploy/systemd/yalla-worker.service`, `deploy/systemd/README.md`, `deploy/systemd/control-plane.env.example`, SECURITY.md, CI, and `scripts/verify.sh` in lockstep; load secrets only from `/etc/yalla/control-plane.env`; preserve separate API/worker units, non-root `User=yalla`, systemd hardening, journald structured logs, API `/healthz` + `/readyz`, and worker no-HTTP-listener health semantics.
 - Kubernetes operations artifacts should be pinned by static release tests and an offline render path: keep `deploy/kubernetes/yalla-control-plane.yaml`, `deploy/kubernetes/README.md`, `deploy/kubernetes/kustomization.yaml`, SECURITY.md, CI, and `scripts/verify.sh` in lockstep; never check in Secret objects; bind runtime credentials from `yalla-control-plane-secrets`; preserve separate API/worker workloads and least-privilege pod security.

